hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-70 = cons "**Continuous sensory and physical streams: cubical boundaries, multi-scale quotient towers, and discrete equivalences.** Flattening an image, audio waveform, video, or field tensor into a 1D byte scan destroys its geometry before compression begins. In a cubical discrete foundation (Part I §3, §7.4 `Tensor`, Appendix A unitary equivalences), higher-dimensional adjacency supplies native k-cell boundary operators: 1-cells are local differences (edges Δ_x, Δ_y, Δ_t), 2-cells are local curvatures (discrete exterior derivatives Δ_xy, Δ_xx), and 3-cells are spatiotemporal transport paths across frames (moving patches carried by transport plus a small residual fiber). Composing these with multi-scale bit-plane quotient towers o₀ → o₁ → … → o_k (`fiberEquiv`) exposes dense exact repeats and symmetries in coarse quotients while encoding fine bit-planes as narrow fibers conditioned on them. Invertible transforms — integer lifting wavelets, linear predictive recurrences, and discrete unitary transforms — enter as first-class equivalences e : A ≃ B (`ua`(e)) in exact discrete integer and rational arithmetic, avoiding continuum real-analysis drift while preserving bit-exact invertibility." (cons "" nil)
